From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:16:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 275/342] usb_audio: a device's name ends at its first NUL

The Y-247A pads its product string with NUL characters, which showed as
question marks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/usb/Device.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/usb/Device.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/usb/Device.cpp
index 0ba520d78e..aea3b48e49 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/usb/Device.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/audio/usb/Device.cpp
@@ -444,6 +444,8 @@ Device::_ReadName(uint8 stringIndex)
 	char name[sizeof(fName)];
 	size_t count = 0;
 	for (size_t i = 2; i + 1 < length; i += 2) {
+		if (descriptor[i] == 0 && descriptor[i + 1] == 0)
+			break;
 		name[count++] = descriptor[i + 1] == 0 && descriptor[i] >= 0x20
 			&& descriptor[i] < 0x7f ? descriptor[i] : '?';
 	}
